ucts\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Build integrations that are resilient, observable, well-governed, and easier for partners to adopt.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-8 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Wolfitpark Editorial · \",\"April 30, 2026\"]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"container-site max-w-3xl py-16\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-7 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"APIs are the connective tissue of modern enterprise architecture. Every integration point is also a potential attack surface, which is why security must be designed into API contracts from the start.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"Adopt a zero-trust model for API design: authenticate every request, authorize against the principle of least privilege, and encrypt all data in transit and at rest. Never assume the safety of the internal network.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":\"Implement rate limiting, throttling, and input validation at the gateway layer. These controls protect against both malicious attacks and unintentional overload from misconfigured clients.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"children\":\"Design for observability: structured logging, request tracing, and metrics that distinguish between client errors, server errors, and security events. Good observability is the foundation of incident response.\"}]]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"section-pad bg-muted/30 border-y border-border\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"container-site\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.22em] text-primary justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2f\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\